## Node name. Distribution listens on loopback only (below), so the node is
## reached from this host as {{name}}@localhost. For a cluster, switch to
## -name {{name}}@<host>, drop inet_dist_use_interface and set RELEASE_COOKIE.
-sname {{name}}@localhost

-kernel inet_dist_use_interface {127,0,0,1}

## Enable kernel poll and SMP
+K true
+A30

## The distribution cookie comes from RELEASE_COOKIE, which every node of a
## cluster sets to the same secret. Unset, the node uses a random
## ~/.erlang.cookie instead. Keep this line last: an empty value then ends the
## arguments rather than taking the next one as the cookie.
-setcookie ${RELEASE_COOKIE}
